  "notes": "Compound of {長|なが} (long) + {居|い} (staying/being). Implies staying longer than socially expected or appropriate.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {長居|ながい}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to overstay)\n- {長居|ながい}⟦して→する：00392_suru⟧すみません (sorry for staying so long)\n- {長居|ながい}⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧{無用|むよう} (no need to stay long — a polite way to suggest leaving)\n\nUSAGE:\n{長居|ながい}⟦して→する：00392_suru⟧すみません is a very common phrase used when leaving someone's home or a shop. It shows awareness that one may have imposed on the host's time or space.",
